# React Native Expo Best Practices

## Project Structure

```
apps/mobile/src/
  api/          # API client, endpoint functions, response types
  auth/         # Auth context & hooks
  components/   # Reusable UI components
  navigation/   # Navigator setup & type definitions
  screens/      # Screen components (one per route)
  storage/      # Secure storage utilities
  theme.ts      # Centralized design tokens
  config.ts     # App configuration
```

New screens go in `screens/`, reusable UI in `components/`, API functions in `api/mobile-api.ts`.

## Styling

Use `StyleSheet.create()` with the centralized theme from `src/theme.ts`. Never use inline style objects or hardcoded colors/spacing.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { theme } from '../theme';

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    padding: theme.spacing.md,
    backgroundColor: theme.colors.green[50],
    borderRadius: theme.borderRadius.md,
  },
});

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded values
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: { padding: 16, backgroundColor: '#F0FDF4', borderRadius: 12 },
});
```

## Components

- Functional components only, with TypeScript props interfaces.
- Use `Pressable` over `TouchableOpacity` for touch interactions.
- Extract reusable UI into `src/components/` with variant/size props.
- Use `useCallback` for handlers passed to child components or FlatList.

## Navigation

- React Navigation v7 with Native Stack.
- Define all route params in `src/navigation/types.ts`.
- Use typed `useNavigation<NativeStackNavigationProp<…>>()` hooks.
- Auth vs Main stacks are conditional on `accessToken` in `AuthContext`.

## API & Data Fetching

- All API calls go through `apiRequest()` from `src/api/client.ts`.
- Add new endpoints as exported functions in `src/api/mobile-api.ts`.
- Define response types in `src/api/types.ts`.
- Fetch data in `useEffect` or `useCallback`; handle loading/error states locally.

```tsx
// ✅ Pattern for screen data fetching
const [data, setData] = useState<MyType | null>(null);
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

const load = useCallback(async () => {
  setLoading(true);
  try {
    const result = await fetchMyData(token);
    setData(result);
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
}, [token]);

useEffect(() => { load(); }, [load]);
```

## State Management

- Use React Context for cross-cutting concerns (auth, drawer).
- Use local `useState` for screen-level state.
- Custom hooks (`useAuth`, `useDrawer`) to access contexts.
- No Redux/Zustand — keep it simple with Context + hooks.

## Security

- Store tokens with `expo-secure-store`, never `AsyncStorage`.
- The API client auto-logs out on 401 responses.
- Never log or expose tokens in error messages.

## General

- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` types.
- Expo SDK ~54; use Expo-compatible packages only.
- French localization for user-facing strings.
- Role-aware UI: check `profile.role` (owner, manager, seller) before rendering privileged features.
